## 1. Artifact contents

```
pasttel-vmcai27-artifact/
├── README                            this file
├── LICENSE                           AGPL-3.0, PaSTTeL's licence (the others: below)
├── VMCAI2027-PAPER.pdf               the paper
├── pasttel-docker-image-vmcai27.tar.gz   the pre-built Docker image (section 2)
├── pasttel-docker-image-vmcai27.tar.gz.sha256   its SHA256 checksum
├── Dockerfile                        the image: install.sh, then the test suite and the smoke test
├── docker-compose.yml                the same image, with Docker Compose
├── package.sh                        builds this archive
│
├── scripts/                          what reviewers run (section 6)
│   ├── run_smoke_test.sh             both comparisons on 10 programs, about 2 min (section 2)
│   ├── run_full_evaluation.sh        both comparisons, full or --subset (sections 3.2, 3.3)
│   ├── run_ulr_vs_pulr.sh            [1] ULR-Baseline vs P-ULR, on any programs or traces
│   ├── run_ulr_vs_upl.sh             [2] Ultimate-LR vs Ultimate-PL, on any programs
│   ├── install.sh                    installation without Docker (section 6)
│   └── common.sh                     paths and the paper's defaults (timeouts, cores)
│
├── pasttel/                          PaSTTeL, C++17
│   ├── src/, include/                sources: techniques, templates, portfolio, SMT solvers, parser
│   ├── examples/                     103 JSON lassos, the paper's Figure 1 among them
│   ├── scripts/                      the analysis scripts (tables, plots) and the test suite
│   ├── Makefile                      builds bin/pasttel and bin/libpasttel.a
│   └── README.md                     PaSTTeL alone: build, options, input, library
│
├── benchmarks/
│   ├── ulr_vs_pulr/                  [1]: 2,856 programs (1,557 C, 1,299 Boogie), Table 1 and Figure 5
│   ├── ulr_vs_upl/                   [2]: 1,087 of them (C/Boogie programs), Figure 6
│   ├── subset/                       --subset (section 3.2)
│   │   ├── ulr_vs_pulr/              360 programs of [1]
│   │   ├── ulr_vs_upl/               100 programs of [2]
│   │   └── select_subsets.py         chooses them from our logs (section 3.2)
│   ├── smoke_test/                   section 2
│   │   ├── full_programs_c_bpl/      the 10 programs
│   │   └── json_lassos_from_full_programs/   their 14 traces, as the JSON PaSTTeL reads
│   └── additional_programs/          574 other programs (C/, BPL/), not used by the experiments
│
├── logs/                             our runs (sections 3.1, 4)
│   ├── results_P-ULR-Seq_z3.csv      [1] per trace, ULR-Baseline and P-ULR-Seq
│   ├── results_P-ULR-Seq_z3_scatter.html    Figure 5
│   ├── results_P-ULR-Par7_z3.csv     [1] per trace, ULR-Baseline and P-ULR-Par7
│   ├── results_P-ULR-Par7_z3_scatter.html   same scatter-plot as Figure 5 for P-ULR-Par7 (not in the paper)
│   ├── results_ULR_vs_UPL.csv        [2] per program
│   ├── results_ULR_vs_UPL_wall.html  [2] Figure 6
│   ├── ULR_vs_PULR_logs.zip          [1] raw: the lasso traces (.txt and .json), Ultimate's logs
│   ├── ULR_vs_UPL_logs.zip           [2] raw: Ultimate's log, wall clock and exit status of each run
│   └── smoke_test_output.log         the smoke test's expected output
│
├── tools/
│   ├── UAutomizer-linux/             Ultimate 0.3.1, the release of [1]: dumps the lasso traces
│   ├── UAutomizer-PaSTTeL-linux/     Ultimate 0.3.2, the release of [2]: PaSTTeL as optional backend
│   ├── settings/
│   │   └── BuchiAutomizerPasttel.epf.in   Ultimate-PL's settings: the PaSTTeL lines only
│   ├── toolchains/                   BuchiAutomizerC.xml and BuchiAutomizerBpl.xml
│   └── solvers/                      the Z3 4.16.0 and CVC5 1.3.4 archives
│
├── ultimate/                         sources of Ultimate 0.3.2 with PaSTTeL (section 6)
└── ultimate-verifier/                sources of Ultimate 0.3.1 with the lasso-trace dump (section 6)
```

The two zips of `logs/` are in the Zenodo archive only. They exceed GitHub's file-size limit, so the
git repository of the paper's footnote has everything else, but not them.

Licences:
- PaSTTeL: AGPL-3.0 (`LICENSE`).
- Ultimate, both releases and both source trees: LGPL-3.0 with a linking exception (`ultimate/README.md`).
- Z3 4.16.0: MIT (`LICENSE.txt` in its archive). CVC5 1.3.4: BSD-3-Clause (`COPYING` in its archive);
  its archive also ships GMP and LibPoly, under the LGPL.
- nlohmann/json, in `pasttel/include/external/`: MIT.
- The benchmark programs come from SV-COMP, TermCOMP (TPDB) and the Ultimate repository, each under
  the licence of its source.

